 "verses": {
  "bsb|HEB 4:6": {
   "text": "Since, then, it remains for some to enter His rest, and since those who formerly heard the good news did not enter because of their disobedience,"
  },
  "bsb|HEB 4:7": {
   "text": "God again designated a certain day as “Today,” when a long time later He spoke through David as was just stated: “Today, if you hear His voice, do not harden your hearts.”"
  },
  "bsb|HEB 4:8": {
   "text": "For if Joshua had given them rest, God would not have spoken later about another day."
  },
  "bsb|HEB 4:9": {
   "text": "There remains, then, a Sabbath rest for the people of God."
  },
  "bsb|JOS 21:44": {
   "text": "And the LORD gave them rest on every side, just as He had sworn to their fathers. None of their enemies could stand against them, for the LORD delivered all their enemies into their hand."
  },
  "bsb|PSA 95:11": {
   "text": "So I swore on oath in My anger, “They shall never enter My rest.”"
  },
  "bsb|PSA 95:7": {
   "text": "For He is our God, and we are the people of His pasture, the sheep under His care. Today, if you hear His voice,"
  },
